<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids firm.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids firm.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids firmed on Thursday but movement remained sluggish, dealers said.</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures edged up 1/2 cent to finish at $4.20-1/2 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;Farmers are still hanging on to their crop,&quot; a Minnesota dealer said.</p>
<p>But dealers said a lot of winter wheat seedings in areas of the northern Plains are delayed due to the lack of moisture. &quot;We have not had (sufficient) rain since May,&quot; a Montana broker said.</p>
<p>Another Montana dealer said some areas were about three weeks late in planting winter wheat.  </p>
